  "scope": "Both existing human outfits: UV-aligned steel/cloth response and a static preview reflection environment. Groom geometry trials were rejected; no body, hair geometry, rig, morph, clip or save schema is replaced.",
  "implemented": [
    "One shared Blender-authored 1024 response map, red metal amount / green roughness; original diffuse, normal, AO, authored UVs and palette remain. Pants/boots stay nonmetallic.",
    "Actual creator gains a static 64px procedural reflection sky while retaining its plain BG_COLOR backdrop, existing ambient color, key and fill lights. No custom sky shader or extra world reflection system is integrated.",
    "A mandatory native gate compares actual rendered material controls, all ten saved cloth palettes, metal/cloth texels, physical mip levels, unchanged backdrop and disabled-versus-enabled reflection pixels. Two actual creator frames are captured.",
    "The actual exported-PCK harness now additionally requires the response texture/mips and creator reflection helper. Every pre-existing gate/assertion is retained."
  ],
